{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116474",
      "title": "Setting & Resolving Titles",
      "lectureOrder": 295,
      "videoOrder": 281,
      "sourceHash": "eba1f0cffc805e0e5a23a27541b499854c54bbb66c5e78f1baf5305916b8e7e4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "Now in Angular, you cannot just resolve data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 9.95,
          "en": "for a component, but also the title for a route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.11,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "Because of course, as you navigate between different routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "you might want to update this page title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 19.11,
          "en": "which for example, shows up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "but which also would show up in search engine results.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 27.03,
          "en": "You might wanna update that as you navigate between routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 29.763,
          "en": "and Angular also helps you with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.81,
          "end": 33.69,
          "en": "For example, Angular allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.69,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "to define a static title property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 39.388,
          "en": "for every route you set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.388,
          "end": 42.36,
          "en": "So you can simply add a title property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 44.4,
          "en": "to your route configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.4,
          "end": 47.313,
          "en": "and then set that to any string of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "Like for example, no task selected here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 53.163,
          "en": "or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.96,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "If I do that, if I add this title property like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 62.22,
          "en": "and I go back to /nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 65.673,
          "en": "you see this title is showing up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.577,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "But it's of course also quite common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 72.6,
          "en": "that you might have some dynamic title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.6,
          "end": 75.532,
          "en": "that depends on some data that was loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.532,
          "end": 79.71000000000001,
          "en": "For example, here when we're on the user tasks component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.71000000000001,
          "end": 80.91,
          "en": "if we're on this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.91,
          "end": 85.35,
          "en": "or one of its child routes, we might want to set a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 89.4,
          "en": "that outputs the user name that was selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.4,
          "end": 92.88300000000001,
          "en": "So setting a static title will no longer do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.72,
          "end": 98.72,
          "en": "But thankfully, title also does not just accept the string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.33,
          "end": 103.533,
          "en": "but also some resolver function or clause.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.78999999999999,
          "end": 108.78,
          "en": "So you can call a function just as you're doing it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.78,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "to set your title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "So for example, here we could go to the user tasks component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 118.949,
          "en": "and add a second resolver function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.949,
          "end": 120.633,
          "en": "which we could name resolveTitle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "which will also be of type ResolveFn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 129.453,
          "en": "and which will also yield a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 133.68,
          "en": "And then here in the end, I also want to have a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.68,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "where I get my activated route and this router state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 142.41,
          "en": "though these type annotations here actually aren't needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 146.46,
          "en": "If you have this annotation, that's all TypeScript needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 149.433,
          "en": "to understand what shape this function should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.45,
          "end": 153.45,
          "en": "And then here, we can of course simply call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 156.57999999999998,
          "en": "our other resolver, resolveUserName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 163.25,
          "en": "and forward our activatedRoute and routerState, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "because that will then give me my user name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "and then simply append some other string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "like for example, 'S Tasks',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "so that overall here in resolve title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 180.48,
          "en": "we can return the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 180.48,
          "end": 182.7,
          "en": "f resolving our user name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 182.7,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "and then concatenate this string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 189.39,
          "en": "so that we overall return a title like max tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 189.39,
          "end": 191.493,
          "en": "or whatever username we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 193.976,
          "end": 196.23,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could also copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 196.23,
          "end": 198.81,
          "en": "and paste this entire code down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 201.453,
          "en": "but that's simply the shorter way of doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 206.67000000000002,
          "en": "Well and with that, we got this resolve title function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 206.67000000000002,
          "end": 207.87,
          "en": "which we're exporting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.87,
          "end": 210.187,
          "en": "and we can therefore go back to our routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.187,
          "end": 214.683,
          "en": "and now set the title here to resolve title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 216.57,
          "end": 218.64,
          "en": "And that now also must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 221.403,
          "en": "from our user tasks component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 225.12,
          "en": "And we need a comma here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 225.12,
          "end": 228.45,
          "en": "But with that, this title will now be set dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.45,
          "end": 230.79399999999998,
          "en": "and that's all you have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 230.79399999999998,
          "end": 233.82,
          "en": "If you do that and you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.82,
          "end": 237.45,
          "en": "if you select a user, you see that title here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.45,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "was updated and represents that user name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 244.74,
          "en": "And if I switch to a different user, the title also updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 244.74,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "So that's working as intended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 251.01,
          "en": "And that's therefore another very useful feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 251.01,
          "end": 252.453,
          "en": "that might come in handy.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
